## 2. Exact current derivation code

### region code — `LocalityResolver.java`
Two tables: `CITY_REGION = {Sydney→NSW, Melbourne→VIC, Brisbane→QLD}`, `KNOWN_REGIONS = {NSW,VIC,QLD}`. Postcode wins over city.
```java
// lines 49-51
public static String resolve(String city, String postcode) {
    return PostcodePolicy.regionForPostcode(postcode).orElseGet(() -> regionForCity(city));
}
// lines 64-67  (used by the DTO mapper)
public static String fromMemberId(String memberId, String city, String postcode) {
    String region = MemberIdGenerator.region(memberId);
    return region != null && !region.isEmpty() ? region : resolve(city, postcode);
}
// lines 76-81
public static String regionForCity(String city) {
    if (city == null) { return UNKNOWN; }
    return CITY_REGION.getOrDefault(city, UNKNOWN);
}
```
`PostcodePolicy.regionForPostcode` (lines 62-77) reverse-maps a 4-digit postcode via ranges `NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099`.

### householdId — `HouseholdIdGenerator.java` (lines 46-49)
```java
public static String generate(String lastName, String postcode) {
    String key = TextNormalizer.normalize(lastName) + SEPARATOR + (postcode == null ? "" : postcode);
    return Sha256.hex(key).substring(0, LENGTH).toUpperCase();  // LENGTH=12, SEPARATOR="|"
}
```
First 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalize(lastName) + "|" + postcode)`, upper-cased. `normalize` = trim + collapse whitespace + lowercase.

### identityKey — `OwnerIdentityKey.java` (lines 46-51)
```java
public static String of(Owner owner) {
    String raw = orEmpty(owner.getTelephone())
        + SEPARATOR + orEmpty(owner.getEmail())
        + SEPARATOR + Soundex.encode(owner.getLastName());   // SEPARATOR="|"
    return Sha256.hex(raw);   // full 64-char lowercase hex
}
```
NOTE: uses `Soundex(lastName)`, not householdId, despite the OpenAPI/exception docs.

### memberId — `MemberIdGenerator.java`
Format `"<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>"`:
```java
// lines 55-59
public static String format(String region, LocalDate registrationDate, String normalizedTelephone, String lastName) {
    String base = region + FiscalYear.twoDigit(registrationDate) + hash8(normalizedTelephone, lastName);
    return base + LuhnCheckDigit.compute(base);
}
// lines 100-103  HASH8 = first 8 upper hex of SHA-256(telephone + lastName)
private static String hash8(String normalizedTelephone, String lastName) {
    String key = orEmpty(normalizedTelephone) + orEmpty(lastName);
    return Sha256.hex(key).substring(0, HASH_LENGTH).toUpperCase();   // HASH_LENGTH=8
}
// lines 70-80  de-dup by appending "-<n>" (n>=2)
public static String deduplicate(String baseMemberId, Predicate<String> isTaken) { ... }
// lines 89-98  region() = leading run of letters
```
Orchestrated in `ClinicServiceImpl.assignMemberId` (lines 341-349): region via `LocalityResolver.resolve(city, postcode)`, then dedup against `ownerRepository.findByMemberIdStartingWith(baseId)`.

`FiscalYear.twoDigit` (fiscal year starts 1 July; `startingYear % 100` zero-padded). `LuhnCheckDigit.compute` = standard Luhn over digits, doubling from rightmost.

### ownerSegment — `OwnerSegment.java` (lines 36-40)
```java
public static String of(int membershipLevel, String locality) {
    String tier = membershipLevel >= 3 ? "PREMIUM" : "STANDARD";
    String area = LocalityResolver.isKnownRegion(locality) ? "METRO" : "REGIONAL";
    return tier + "_" + area;   // e.g. STANDARD_METRO
}
```

### timezone — `TimezoneResolver.forRegion` (lines 42-44): fixed map `NSW→Australia/Sydney, VIC→Australia/Melbourne, QLD→Australia/Brisbane`, else `null`.

### Where memberId/householdId are set at create time — `ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner` (lines 279-309)
```java
owner.setHouseholdId(HouseholdIdGenerator.generate(owner.getLastName(), owner.getPostcode()));
rejectIdentityCollision(owner);                 // hard duplicate check (identityKey)
...
owner.setMemberId(assignMemberId(owner));       // region+FY+hash8+chk, deduped
ownerRepository.save(owner);
ownerAuditLogger.ownerCreated(owner);
welcomeNotifier.welcome(owner);
return owner.getHouseholdId();
```
`rejectIdentityCollision` (317-325): compares `OwnerIdentityKey.of` against active owners sharing telephone → throws `DuplicateOwnerException`. `flagPossibleDuplicate`/`findSoftMatchCandidates` (361-386): soft match on same postcode + same Soundex(lastName) but different identityKey.

---

## 3. Current owner response shape / DTO

Generated `OwnerDto` = `OwnerFields` + Owner-specific fields (openapi.yml lines 1991-2352). Fields, all `readOnly` unless noted:

Editable (`OwnerFields`, also the request body): `firstName`, `lastName`, `title`(MR/MRS/MS/DR), `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, `city`, `telephone`, `email`, `postcode`(`^[0-9]{4}$`), `registrationDate`, `birthDate`, `sharesHousehold`(writeOnly, not persisted). Required: firstName, lastName, city, telephone.

Owner response-only fields (flat, top-level):
`id`, `selfLink`, `displayName`, `salutation`, `initials`, `telephoneDisplay`, **`memberId`**, **`householdId`**, **`identityKey`**, `namesakeCount`, `fiscalYear`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`(1-4), **`locality`**, **`timezone`**, `contactPreference`(EMAIL/PHONE), **`ownerSegment`**, `ageBand`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `riskFlag`, `deleted`, `pets`(required).

The derived-field wiring lives in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` (`OwnerMapper.java` lines 21-51) via MapStruct `expression=` calls, e.g.:
```java
@Mapping(target = "locality", expression = "java(...LocalityResolver.fromMemberId(owner.getMemberId(), owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode()))")
@Mapping(target = "timezone", expression = "java(...TimezoneResolver.forRegion(...LocalityResolver.fromMemberId(...)))")
@Mapping(target = "ownerSegment", expression = "java(...OwnerSegment.of(...OwnerMembership.level(owner), ...LocalityResolver.fromMemberId(...)))")
@Mapping(target = "identityKey", expression = "java(...OwnerIdentityKey.of(owner))")
```
Note: `locality`/`timezone`/`ownerSegment` on responses derive the region from `memberId` (via `fromMemberId`), falling back to city/postcode; whereas at create time `memberId` itself is built from `LocalityResolver.resolve(city, postcode)`.

`OwnerPage` (openapi.yml 2353+): `content[]`, `page`, `size`, `totalElements`, `totalPages` — mapped by `OwnerMapper.toOwnerPageDto` (lines 73-81), served by `OwnerRestControllerV2`.

---

## 4. Audit event class/schema and how it's built

### `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` (record, lines 31-38)
```java
public record OwnerCreatedEvent(long seq, Integer ownerId, String memberId, int membershipLevel, String event) {
    public static final String EVENT_TYPE = "OWNER_CREATED";
    public OwnerCreatedEvent(long seq, Integer ownerId, String memberId, int membershipLevel) {
        this(seq, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, EVENT_TYPE);
    }
}
```
Serialized to JSON: `{"seq","ownerId","memberId","membershipLevel","event":"OWNER_CREATED"}`.

### `OwnerAuditLogger.java` (lines 51-69)
```java
public void ownerCreated(Owner owner) {
    AUDIT.info("Owner created: id={} memberId={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId(), owner.getRegistrationDate(), membershipLevel(owner));
    OwnerCreatedEvent event = new OwnerCreatedEvent(
        sequence.incrementAndGet(), owner.getId(), primaryIdentifier(owner), membershipLevel(owner));
    AUDIT.info(EVENT_MAPPER.writeValueAsString(event));
}
private static String primaryIdentifier(Owner owner) { return owner.getMemberId(); }
private static int membershipLevel(Owner owner) { return OwnerMembership.level(owner); }
```
Emits two lines to the `AUDIT` logger: a human-readable line and the JSON event. `primaryIdentifier` = `memberId`. Uses Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson.databind`). `membershipLevel` via `OwnerMembership.level` (stored capped level, else natural). **There is no owner-segment field in the audit event** — segment derivation (`OwnerSegment`) is only in the DTO mapper, not the audit path. The audit event's only "segment-like" datum is `membershipLevel`.

---

## 5. Test files referencing these things

### `AcceptanceTest.java` (full — asserts a TARGET nested-identity v2 shape not yet implemented)
```java
/** identity-v2: apiVersion is 2, the memberId/identityKey/householdId are grouped under a nested
 * 'identity' object, and those three are no longer at the top level. Exact structural contract. */
@Test
void coreV2GroupsIdentityAndVersions() throws Exception {
    int id = createOwnerOk(structuredOwner());
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.apiVersion").value(2))
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.identity.memberId").isNotEmpty())
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.identity.identityKey").isNotEmpty())
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.identity.householdId").isNotEmpty())
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.memberId").doesNotExist())
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.identityKey").doesNotExist())
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$.householdId").doesNotExist());
}
```

### `AcceptanceBase.java` — pinned reference tables + replicated algorithms
- Lines 227-242: `CITY_REGION`, `REGION_TIMEZONE`, `REGION_POSTCODES` (2000-2099 etc.), `HOLIDAYS` — mirror the production tables exactly.
- Lines 244-256: `region(city)`, `timezone(city)`, `validPostcode(city)`.
- Lines 282-321: `sha256hex`, `shaHex(s,n)` (first n upper hex), `luhn(s)` — the test's independent reimplementations used to compute expected memberId/householdId/identityKey.
- Lines 116-142: payload builders `ownerNode()`, `withPostcode()`, `structuredOwner()` (postcode "2000").
- Lines 155-197: `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk`/`createOwnerWithKey`/`getOwner`/`deleteOwner`.

### `AuditLogCapture.java` (full)
Test utility attaching a Logback `ListAppender` to the `AUDIT` logger; `messages()`, `anyContains(...)`, `anyAtLevel(level,...)`, `count()`. Used to assert `OwnerAuditLogger` output including the `OWNER_CREATED` JSON.

---

## 6. Request DTOs

- **`OwnerFieldsDto`** (generated from `OwnerFields`, openapi.yml 1991-2117): the create/update request body. Fields listed in section 3. Class-level annotations `@ValidPostcodeForCity @ValidAddressForm`; field-level `@TelephoneDigits`, `@Email`, `@PastOrPresent`. `sharesHousehold` is `writeOnly` (request-only, drives the declared-household-member path in `createOwner`).
- Consumed in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (lines 118-135) and `updateOwner` (139-157) via `ownerMapper.toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (`OwnerMapper.java` lines 55-67), which normalizes telephone→E.164, lowercases email, composes/normalizes address. Note: `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` does NOT set memberId/householdId/identityKey — those are computed later in `ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`.
- No dedicated request DTO carries identity fields; identity is entirely server-derived.

